#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""v345-Q — al-Maqṣūd's open rule units, applied: each unit's rule is run through the engine on the BOOK'S OWN words — the vowelled
example of the unit itself or of the passage that states it (the line is named in `src`). The reading (root, door, variant) is ours and is
fixed here, never guessed by a runner: a homograph (اِسْتَجَدَ is also VIII of س ج د) would otherwise prove the wrong bāb.

    python3 tools/ledger/maqsud_hand_probes.py      → tools/ledger/maqsud_hand_probes.json (sarf_probe_run.js reads it as its hand list)
Every word is checked here to stand VERBATIM in the cited line of research/sources/maqsud-sarf.txt.
Probe kinds (tools/ledger/sarf_probe_eval.js): mqr {root, key, variant?, w} = a cell of MaqsudEngine.recite; ilal {asl, w} = IlalEngine.derive
spells the book's word from the book's aṣl; kept {asl, gate} = the word is kept, the named gate blocking; js {expr, want}.
"""
